# Normalize line endings and pin source files to UTF-8.
#
# Why this file exists: commit 964271c and merge fc4e1c7 were produced on a
# machine whose editor/merge tool round-tripped UTF-8 source through CP949,
# silently garbling every Korean string in Falsification.tsx and
# SettlementModal.tsx (see src/lib/__tests__/mojibake-guard.test.ts for the
# runtime defense). git can't validate encodings by itself, but declaring
# text+eol here stops CRLF/encoding-transparent tools from rewriting whole
# files, which is how the corruption slipped past review as a "changed file".
* text=auto eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
